==============================================================================
PROBE 0 -- the three affine identities (exact, 60000 random cases each)
==============================================================================
    orientR (A + e*E) B C = orientR A B C + e * cross E (B - C)
    orientR A (B + e*E) C = orientR A B C + e * cross E (C - A)
    orientR A B (C + e*E) = orientR A B C + e * cross (B - A) E
    mismatches: [0, 0, 0]   (all three must be 0)
    CONSEQUENCES used below:
      * P-side k = i   : moving endpoint is P[i] (the FIRST argument),
        coefficient = cross(E, P[i+1] - X)
      * P-side k = i-1 : moving endpoint is P[i] (the SECOND argument),
        coefficient = cross(E, X - P[i-1])
      * Q-side j       : the moving point is the THIRD argument,
        coefficient = cross(Q[j+1] - Q[j], E)

