==============================================================================
E2 -- CLAIM C, the three-case characterisation, at scale (small e only)
==============================================================================
    (a) Q[j] = the FIXED endpoint of the incident side -> survives always
    (b) cross(E, Fixed - Q[j]) != 0, i.e. E NOT parallel to the side
           -> dies for every e != 0
    (c) E parallel to the side -> dies only if Q[j] = P[i] and e*E points
           strictly from P[i] towards the fixed endpoint
    segDegP mirror: (b') cross(Q[j+1]-Q[j], E) != 0 -> dies;
           (c') E parallel to the Q-side -> dies only if P[i] is an
           endpoint of that Q-side and e*E points outward
